[{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n0","normalized_index":0,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"generate_single_script must obtain agent data by calling get_agent_data(overall_goal, ',') instead of using call_llm_with_retry","justification":"The core obligation is that generate_single_script must call get_agent_data(overall_goal, ',') rather than call_llm_with_retry, which is a choice of which API element to invoke (API Element Selection). The error-logging, ValueError on empty response, and re-raise details are secondary. They are not clearly covered by another leaf: SAM.SE concerns caller-observable state effects, and no argument-value constraint is stated. The 'instead of' framing makes element selection the dominant obligation.","leaf_id":"MINT.AES","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n1","normalized_index":1,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"calculate_max_response_tokens must return openai_max_tokens minus the prompt's token count minus a 200-token reserve. When that value is negative, it must log an error and return 0.","justification":"The contract specifies the value one method returns: openai_max_tokens minus the prompt token count minus a 200-token reserve, clamped to 0 when negative. This is a postcondition on the returned value, so it fits Return Value Contract. The error log is secondary to the return guarantee, so SAM.SE is not the primary fit. It is not an argument constraint (SAM.BET.*), because it describes output rather than input values.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.RV","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n2","normalized_index":2,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"return the crew name and the remaining stripped lines, each prefixed with the double-quoted crew name and a comma, joined and terminated by newlines.","justification":"The contract is a postcondition of the single method extract_csv_data on what it returns: (None, None) in the rejection cases, otherwise the crew name plus the remaining lines, each prefixed with the quoted crew name and a comma, newline-joined and terminated. This constrains returned content and structure, so MINT.SAM.RV fits. The filename and GREEK_ALPHABETS conditions only determine which return form applies. They are not a separate argument-value contract (SAM.BET.IC1), because the primary obligation is the returned value. No state or side effect is involved (SAM.SE).","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.RV","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n3","normalized_index":3,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"It must return both the combined CSV text and a JSON string of its records as header-keyed objects.","justification":"The obligation is a postcondition of a single method, concatenate_crew_data, on the value it returns: combined CSV text with a specific quoted header, newline-separated rows in input order, and a JSON string of header-keyed records. This constrains the structure and content of the return value, not an argument, call order, or side effect. SAM.SE does not apply because no state or file is written. XCD does not apply because the data flow from extract_csv_data is internal to the function and no value must be forwarded between caller-visible calls.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.RV","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n4","normalized_index":4,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"The ranking prompt must embed:
- the number of distinct crews and their names;
- the overall goal;
- the actual JSON data string of the concatenated crews, not a literal placeholder;","justification":"The obligation is a postcondition of a single method, construct_ranking_prompt, on the value it returns. The returned prompt must contain specific content: the distinct crew count and names, the goal, the actual JSON data rather than a placeholder, and a ranking request. Crew names are derived from path basenames with order-preserving deduplication, which is also part of the returned content. It is not an argument type or value constraint (SAM.DT/BET) and not a side effect (SAM.SE). It does not span multiple calls, so it is not XCD. The returned content guarantee is argument-independent, which fits the RV inclusion criterion on content guarantees.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.RV","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n5","normalized_index":5,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"If neither selected backend is available, it must log an error and return an empty list without calling an LLM.","justification":"The contract describes internal backend dispatch in rank_crews: llm_endpoint value and backend availability determine which LLM backend is called, with an error log and empty list otherwise. It is not about the caller's arguments or call order, so SAM.BET.IC1, AMO and H.SAI do not fit. MINT.AES covers which element the API caller must use, not internal routing by the method itself. It is not a return-value-only guarantee, so MINT.SAM.RV does not fit. The excerpt, which concerns CSV prompt text, does not support any other leaf. The environment-dependent availability of the backend is secondary to the internal selection logic, so MINT.EP does not apply either. MINT.SAM.SE does not fit because the error log is incidental to the dispatch.","leaf_id":null,"status":"unclassified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":"no-matching-leaf"},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n6","normalized_index":6,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"It must return the first choice's message content with surrounding whitespace stripped.","justification":"The contract describes the internal implementation of get_openai_response: how it builds its client and request (configured model, fixed system message, prompt, max_tokens) and post-processes the return value. These are implementation steps in the function body, not obligations on a caller. MINT.SAM.RV does not fit because the contract states no caller-facing guarantee about the returned value's type, shape, or content; stripping whitespace from the first choice's content is a processing step of the function itself. SAM.BET and MINT.SAM.PS do not fit because the contract constrains no argument value or parameter signature for callers. MINT.XCD does not fit because it requires a value to be forwarded across distinct API calls by the caller, which is not the case here. MINT.SAM.SE does not fit because the contract describes no observable side effect. The evidence excerpt concerns a CSV prompt rewrite in core.py and does not address this function.","leaf_id":null,"status":"unclassified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":"no-matching-leaf"},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n7","normalized_index":7,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"rank_crews must return the pair produced by process_ranking_response","justification":"The obligation is a postcondition on the value returned by one method (rank_crews): it must return the pair produced by process_ranking_response, with a specified structure (a singleton list of a tuple, and a summary string built from the prefix, CSV paths and ranking response). This constrains the shape and content of the return value, so it fits Return Value Contract. XCD was considered because the value comes from another call, but the obligation is about what is returned rather than which value is forwarded into a call's argument. The source excerpt (a prompt-text diff) does not bear on the obligation.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.RV","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-yanniedog-Autocrew-7a5b47b1ede4cc7eaf96a84e08283b0bb0ce42f1-annotation-4e70b0a283593c2b_n8","normalized_index":8,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"save_ranking_output must write one CSV row per supplied (crew_name, ranking) entry and must not prepend a "crew_name","ranking" header row.","justification":"The obligation describes the observable output the method writes to a CSV file: one row per supplied entry and no header row. This is a caller-observable file-content effect of a single method that does not depend on any argument value, matching the State and Side-Effect Postcondition leaf, whose inclusion criteria give the example of a CSV written without a header row. It is not a return-value contract, since the output is written to a file rather than returned. It is not an argument type or value constraint either.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.SE","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null}]

[{"contract_id":"github-commit-startino-aitino-849d313412c524b98951bb1906536666dd9c7901-annotation-e469090124a43934_n0","normalized_index":0,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"if ($nodes.length >= AGENT_LIMIT) {
			toast.error(`You have reached the maximum limit of ${AGENT_LIMIT} agents.`);
			return;
		}","justification":"The obligation is a postcondition of the single method addAgent. When the node count is already at or above AGENT_LIMIT (receiver/environment state, not an argument value), the crew nodes stay unchanged and an error toast (a caller-observable notification) is shown. This matches the state and side-effect postcondition. It is not a return value contract, since nothing returned is constrained. It is not SAM.BET, since the condition depends on current state rather than an argument value.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.SE","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-startino-aitino-849d313412c524b98951bb1906536666dd9c7901-annotation-e469090124a43934_n1","normalized_index":1,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"if ($nodes.find((node) => node.id === agent.id)) {
			toast.error(
				`Agent is already in the crew. We are working on supporting multiple of the same agent...`
			);
			return;","justification":"The obligation is a postcondition of one method, addAgent: when the crew already contains a node with the agent's id, the crew nodes stay unchanged and an error toast is shown. These are caller-observable state and notification effects, and they depend on the receiver's current state (existing nodes), not on an argument value in the SAM.BET sense. It is not a return value, because the method returns nothing. It is not an argument constraint (SAM.BET.IC1), because the condition is on crew state rather than on a value the caller supplies. It is not an ordering constraint, because no call sequence is required.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.SE","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-startino-aitino-849d313412c524b98951bb1906536666dd9c7901-annotation-e469090124a43934_n2","normalized_index":2,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"addAgent must keep the existing nodes and append a new node to the crew nodes store.","justification":"The obligation describes caller-observable effects of the single method addAgent: appending a node with specified fields to the nodes store while keeping existing nodes, and showing a success toast. These are state and notification side effects, not a returned value, argument constraint, or call ordering. The conditions (limit and duplicate checks) depend on receiver state, not a specific argument value. The requirement to call addAgent when loading is incidental to the postcondition and does not make it an ordering contract (AMO) or element selection (AES).","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.SE","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null}]

[{"contract_id":"github-commit-USP-Open-Code-icmc-open-chatbot-3f30d169ea9d08bf8ca40d3c6ffa18a80ac7d0a0-annotation-580e83cd93345897_n0","normalized_index":0,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"CustomToolNode.__init__ must register those same operations in its tools mapping under "retriever" and "most_recent_files", respectively, so that tool calls emitted by the model are executed.","justification":"The obligation is that the same set of operations passed to the model via bind_tools in the agent node must also be registered in CustomToolNode's tools mapping, so tool calls the model emits can be executed. The substance is consistency of which values (tools) flow between two different calls/components, not call order. This fits Cross-Call Value Dependency. It is not AES, since it does not say which element to use in place of another, and not SAM.PS or SAM.DT.RT, since no single call's argument type or name is constrained. It is not AMO, since no temporal ordering is required.","leaf_id":"MINT.XCD","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-USP-Open-Code-icmc-open-chatbot-3f30d169ea9d08bf8ca40d3c6ffa18a80ac7d0a0-annotation-580e83cd93345897_n1","normalized_index":1,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":""document": (
                    d.page_content
                    if not isinstance(d, dict)
                    else d["page_content"]
                ),","justification":"The obligation concerns how grade_documents (caller-side code) extracts text from its own document item, using dict key access versus attribute access, before passing it to retrieval_grader_chain.invoke. It is not an argument type constraint on invoke (the argument is a string), not a return value contract of an API method (the dict-or-object data is a caller-side component's data, which RV explicitly excludes), and not a parameter name, state, ordering, or cross-call dependency obligation. The closest candidates, SAM.DT.BIT/SAM.DT.RT (type of the document) and MINT.SAM.RV (access form), do not fit because the dict/object duality concerns an internal local value rather than an argument constraint or a method's return, so no existing leaf adequately represents it.","leaf_id":null,"status":"unclassified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":"no-matching-leaf"},{"contract_id":"github-commit-USP-Open-Code-icmc-open-chatbot-3f30d169ea9d08bf8ca40d3c6ffa18a80ac7d0a0-annotation-580e83cd93345897_n2","normalized_index":2,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"grade_documents must retain a document in filtered_docs only when the grader result is truthy and its binary_score attribute equals the string "yes".","justification":"The obligation is a postcondition of the single method grade_documents on a caller-observable effect other than its return value: which documents get retained in filtered_docs (a state the method builds up) depends on the grader result being truthy with binary_score equal to "yes". It is not a constraint on an argument type or value (SAM.DT/BET), since the grader result is produced internally by the chain rather than passed in. It is not a return value contract (RV) because it concerns what is retained in filtered_docs, not the shape of the return. It also does not concern call ordering or cross-call value flow.","leaf_id":"MINT.SAM.SE","status":"classified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":null},{"contract_id":"github-commit-USP-Open-Code-icmc-open-chatbot-3f30d169ea9d08bf8ca40d3c6ffa18a80ac7d0a0-annotation-580e83cd93345897_n3","normalized_index":3,"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5:batch","execution_status":"succeeded","competing_leaf_ids":[],"evidence_quote":"the query must be taken from state.get("query") when that value is truthy. When it is missing or falsy, generate must fall back to messages[0].content.","justification":"The obligation describes internal implementation logic in generate: how a local variable 'query' is derived from state with a fallback to messages[0].content. It is not an argument type/value constraint (the state is one argument, but the obligation is about internal derivation, not a requirement on the caller), not a return value or caller-observable side effect, not a call order, and not a cross-call value dependency. Internal local variable initialization is explicitly out of scope per the SE and XCD exclusions, so no existing leaf fits.","leaf_id":null,"status":"unclassified","taxonomy_hash":"10354551384600ca0c8488e873588e35f50472b08a747f19a88d32bfcaf75b7e","taxonomy_version":"mint_final","unclassified_reason":"no-matching-leaf"}]
